{
  "_name": "t89_hashlocate_warm_shortcircuit",
  "_desc": "H hash-locate (Phase D send-by-hash) live gate. alice(1)-carol(2)-bob(3) CHAIN (alice has NO direct link to bob). alice send_hash bob: alice does not know bob, so it PARKS the DM + floods a SOFT H query; carol \u2014 which learned bob from his first-hand beacon \u2014 answers AUTHORITATIVE and SUPPRESSES the flood (it never reaches bob: zero h_rx at bob, zero h_forward anywhere); alice caches the answer + drains the parked DM, which routes alice->carol->bob. The SECOND send_hash resolves straight from alice cache: NO second flood (h_tx stays at 1) \u2014 the cache-on-pass efficiency payoff (t88-style: repeat by-hash sends do not re-redirect).",
